 The first production review passes 48/53; all 44 prior checks pass. Two failures are locator assumptions (More changes to Less; exact wrapping-label text includes options). Three expose a native shortcut conflict: Space on a card button is consumed by the document listener before native activation, despite React stopPropagation. Native shortcuts now skip card targets explicitly; native button activation and card Escape handling retain ownership. Locator fixes retain focus/expanded/unit assertions, and mobile tests retain paused time and add Escape-close focus restoration. Verification remains 372 plus two expected rejections. A fresh production run checks the nine card cases before full regression. Failed evidence is preserved; P4.6 remains unaccepted.
 
 P4.6 retry is reviewed accepted: nine focused and 53 full production cases pass, source/evidence/log checks and preserved precision/storage/budgets pass. Seven captures were inspected; supplementary unchanged-build Peek captures wait finite CSS transitions after asserting state, avoiding transient background colors in the original captures. Final hashed evidence is in docs/perf/phase-four/p4-6-final-review.json. No frame callback, scientific provider, physical model, engine assets or extra React cadence was introduced. Final shell/clutter and performance gates remain P4.7–P4.9.
+
+P4.6 is committed locally as 36f7a9852acf2e2a62be39fab4d24b5533572767. P4.7 implements the default six-control shell: search, layers, settings, honest closed Happening now, play/pause and date/time. Branding is static; secondary navigation, share, help, scale/frame/view and previous/overview commands live in Settings or the selected card. The unavailable Objects in view action is explicitly disabled until P4.8.
+
+Version-1 local preferences validate only distance units, requested quality and System/On/Off motion; semantic URL fields are excluded. Blocked/corrupt storage falls back to defaults/in-memory changes. The engine bridge restores preferences before the first scheduled consumer frame and owns the system-motion listener and cleanup. Labs retain their accepted setup. Requested quality and active adaptive tier are labelled separately. Reduced motion governs public camera commands and clock LIVE transitions; existing animated/fade behavior remains when motion is enabled. A clamp notice is retained while paused at the same boundary and clears after a valid explicit time command.
+
+The first P4.7 production probe passed 19/20 checks, with a missed clamp notice in the Tokyo timezone case; the full 64-case regression did not run. The simulation paused correctly, but the one-tick clamp flag could clear before a throttled event. The cold clock adapter now recognizes a paused outward boundary following playback, preserves explicit command intent across route snapshot ticks, and resets after a deliberate date/LIVE command. Six deterministic checks exercise the real clock at both boundaries and between its existing 4 Hz samples. No additional subscription, engine frame or scientific change is introduced. Acceptance requires a fresh isolated production retry.
+
+Retry-1 passes the 20 focused checks and 61/64 full cases, with three failures preserved. Closing popover autofocus could steal focus from a newly opened surface; the common closing guard now preserves a connected active element elsewhere while ordinary body fallback still restores the trigger. Diagnosis reproduces the original Layers → Settings → Graphics → Layers race and the corrected stable Settings activation. The lab regression now selects through local search instead of requiring a removed default Mars button. The Reverse regression awaits its actual external/Next-internal URL replacement pair instead of a fixed delay, then requires zero further writes. Playback/history implementation and all timing/scientific gates remain unchanged; P4.7 awaits corrected production review.
+
+Layers read the public requested/available/loaded/visible snapshots through existing notifications and show every known label, including disabled future datasets. Time is UTC in every timezone; the expanded panel contains LIVE, reverse, eight speeds and supported date bounds. Native document shortcuts skip interactive/panel/card targets. Field guide and fallback share dialogs return focus to their actual trigger, or Settings when its action is no longer mounted. View-preset commands preserve selection and explicitly avoid camera-history entries.
+
+Mobile time sits above the bottom sheet; a card ResizeObserver updates a CSS height variable without React commits or a frame loop. A visual-viewport adapter keeps height/top bounds current for resizing/keyboard layouts and cleans up. Popover height also respects Radix's available collision space: an initial short-screen probe found the dismiss target below the viewport; capping to the available height restores internal scrolling and dismissal. Quick corrected probes at 390x844, 390x430 and 844x390 confirm UTC changes, touch controls and timeline/sheet separation. Production validation remains pending: verification is 390 plus two expected rejections in 43 files; twelve specs discover 64 cases, including eleven new controls/mobile cases and all 53 earlier regressions. Existing assertions are retained while opening controls from their new panels. No engine hot-loop/provider/physics/assets change, dependency addition, new independent React cadence or Phase 4B work.
